# Guardrails

## The gate

- Run `pnpm check` before every push and push only when it is green. It runs `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm format:check`, `pnpm check:config` and `pnpm test`.
- Treat it as the only gate. The image build runs `pnpm build` alone, which type-checks but does not lint, format-check or test, and `azure-pipelines.yml` sets `pr: none`, so no pipeline validates a pull request.
- Leave zero lint warnings. The house rules in `eslint.config.mjs` warn until the existing code meets them and then become errors; treat every warning as one now.
- Never silence a check inline: no `eslint-disable`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error` or `prettier-ignore`, and no `.only` or unconditional `.skip`. A real exception goes in `eslint.config.mjs`, scoped to its files, with its reason in a comment.
  YES: move the latest-value read into `useEffectEvent`. NO: `// eslint-disable-next-line react-hooks/exhaustive-deps`.
- Let `pnpm format` write the formatting that `pnpm format:check` reads.

## The guard tests

They scan the source tree and fail the gate. Fix the code they name; never loosen a pattern, raise a limit or skip one.

- `components/admin/fail-closed.test.ts`: no query before a gate decides, and the permission maps.
- `components/xms/function-length.test.ts`: no component or hook of 200 lines or more.
- `components/xms/house-copy.test.ts`, `surfaces.test.tsx` and `panel.test.tsx` beside it: copy, surfaces and panels.
- `styles/tokens/tokens.test.ts`, `lib/safe-url.test.ts`, `lib/routes.test.ts`, `proxy.test.ts`, `next.config.test.ts`, `components/portal/portal-links.test.ts`, `test-kit/shared-fixtures.test.ts` and `scripts/check-next-config.mjs`.

An exemption list only shrinks. `ALLOWED` in `function-length.test.ts` must list the over-long functions exactly, so lower or delete an entry when you shorten one, and never add an entry or raise a number. `WIRE_CONTRACTS` in `house-copy.test.ts` is closed at five.
YES: extract a child out of `CaseForm` and lower its entry from 305. NO: add an entry so a new 230-line component passes.

## The change

- One concern per change: a refactor, a feature and a rename are three commits.
- The app runs on nine runtime dependencies, with no UI kit, date library or CSS-in-JS. Add one only with its reason in the commit body.

## What to update in the same change

- A screen: its row in `SCREENS` in `lib/routes.ts`, with `permission` set to the page's gate key, and a page that renders `<AdminGate>` around a child holding the queries (`gating.mdc`). A portal page gets its row in `PORTAL_SCREENS`, which names it for telemetry only.
- A hook that reads a route behind a permission: its read in the matching map in `components/admin/fail-closed.test.ts`, and every file that calls it among that map's surfaces.
- An API route: the endpoint in its `redux/<area>Api.ts`, any new tag type in `tagTypes` in `redux/api.ts`, a slice test asserting the path, query and body, and a `describe...Error` case with a test for each refusal code it answers with (`data-layer.mdc`).
- A portal link: a literal `href="/portal/..."` must name a page that exists.
